// @@@ If the index is valid (non-negative and less than the size of the vector), then for every element from the position just after the index to the end of the vector, if the element was initially null it remains null, or else it remains unchanged.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is non-negative and less than the size of the vector, then for every index 'i' greater than the specified index and less than the size of the vector, the element at index 'i' is either null if it was null before the operation, or remains unchanged from its previous value.
